{"query":"Property Rates  official site amenities","follow_up_questions":null,"answer":null,"images":[],"results":[{"url":"https://www.bajajfinserv.in/property-rates-in-chennai","title":"Property Rates in Chennai - Real Estate Price & Trends in 2024","content":"Explore current property rates in Chennai effortlessly through our website ... Amenities like swimming pools, gyms, parks, security systems, and parking","score":0.38532895,"raw_content":null,"id":"cde219-00"},{"url":"https://www.99acres.com/property-rates-and-price-trends-in-delhi-prffid","title":"Property Rates in Delhi Aug-2026 - Property Prices / Real Estate Trends in Delhi","content":"## About Delhi Property rates\n\nOne of the largest housing markets in India, Delhi attracts both investors and end-users. The city offers a plethora of employment avenues, social amenities, and recreational options. A wide network of national highways, including NH-44, NH-44, NH-48, NH-9, and NE-3, offer connectivity here. In addition, Delhi Metro connects the city with prominent parts of NCR such as Ghaziabad, Gurgaon, Faridabad, and Noida.\n\nDelhi, a popular employment hub [...] Safdarjung (23.2%), Safdarjung Enclave (23.2%), South Extension 2 (20.4%), Hauz Khas (13.2%), New Friends Colony (12.3%) are some of the areas that offer highest rental returns in Delhi.\n\nQ. What are the factors that influence property rates in Delhi?\n\nSeveral factors influence property rates in Delhi. The key factors include the location's proximity to amenities, infrastructure development, demand and supply dynamics, economic growth, and the overall real estate market conditions.\n\n#### Related to your search\n\nfor fast & easy information regarding Delhi\n\n### Popular Localities in Delhi\n\n### Most Appreciated Localities in Delhi for Flats/Apartments (In 1 Year)\n\n### Most Appreciated Localities in Delhi for Plots/Land (In 1 Year) [...] Property rates in South Delhi\n\nNeb Sarai, Chattarpur, Rajpur Khurd, and Ghitorni are among the affordable areas in South Delhi which have property rates under Rs 9,000 per sq ft. Areas that fall in the mid-segment budget, including Saket, Sarita Vihar, Jasola, and Lajpat Nagar, have property prices within Rs 9,000 per sq ft to Rs 13,000 per sq ft. With housing units starting Rs 13,000 per sq ft, Vasant Vihar, Greater Kailash, Vasant Kunj, Green Park, and Defence Colony are classified as premium localities.\n\nProperty rates in West Delhi","score":0.23911873,"raw_content":null,"id":"4f65d4-01"},{"url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/pune/pcmc-property-tax-on-common-amenities-draws-flak-from-housing-societies/articleshow/131643576.cms","title":"PCMC property tax on common amenities draws flak from housing ...","content":"Several societies have recently received property tax bills ranging from Rs 1 lakh to Rs 5 lakh for common amenities such as clubhouses,","score":0.21800311,"raw_content":null,"id":"d111da-02"},{"url":"https://www.bhumiboss.com/content/hyderabad-real-estate-pricing","title":"An Overview of Hyderabad's Residential Real Estate Prices","content":"Amenities Charges: Usually ranges from ₹100 to ₹600 per sq. ft. and is charged for the development and maintenance of common facilities like the clubhouse,","score":0.16783185,"raw_content":null,"id":"0fd135-03"},{"url":"https://niua.in/sites/default/files/2025-07/2019_1_Assessing%20the%20Importance.pdf","title":"[PDF] Assessing the Importance of Natural Amenities in Terms of Property ...","content":"percent increase in values to homes with a view of a lake. Given that housing prices reflect the value of the property (land and structure) and the amenities available to the homeowners, the price reflects both the property itself and the amenities available. Other things being equal, an increase in home values from amenities, expressed on an annual basis, reflects the yearly value of these amenities. [...] Gandhi et al (2016) study the factors that affect property prices in Mumbai suburbs with a focus on the impact of an upcoming metro line in the vicinity by deploying a hedonic pricing model. Using the OLS regression method, they find that property prices vary with the distance from the CBD as well as land use mix and amenities. The property prices show variation up to 52 percent due to the surroundings like residential built-up areas, commercial areas, open spaces and other amenities in and around the property.\nIn summary, Indian literature also implies an association between the existence of natural amenities (as well as infrastructure services) and residential property values to indicate a premium of property value associated with them. [...] properties. Under the hedonic pricing approach, the various determinants of property prices in urban areas such as external and internal amenities, location of the property, type of property, orientation of property, natural amenities, social and physical infrastructure, etc. are considered. In particular, we examine the value impact of the access to natural amenity, which was positive in the case of several international empirical studies reviewed above. Hence, in the current study, the various factor determinants that affect house/property prices were selected from literature review to perform further analysis and model estimation. The factors/attributes and variables that were short-listed for inclusion are shown in Table 1.","score":0.1636996,"raw_content":null,"id":"813d17-04"},{"url":"https://www.onecityproperty.com/news/bangalore-property-prices-area-wise-complete-guide","title":"Bangalore Property Rates 2026: 30 Localities Compared","content":"### Budget-Wise Property Options in Bangalore\n\nUnder ₹50 Lakhs\n\nFor buyers with a tighter budget, under ₹50 lakhs usually means looking at compact 1 or 2 BHK units in emerging locations or slightly older resale flats in developed areas. On the outskirts and select pockets of North, West and South, you can still find affordable bangalore property in well-planned layouts and modest gated communities. At this price, it is important to prioritize legal clarity, basic amenities, water supply, and future connectivity over luxury features. A realistic mindset on size and distance from core IT hubs is essential.\n\n₹50 Lakhs – ₹1 Crore [...] Green buildings are another strong shift. Projects with more natural light, cross ventilation, solar power, rainwater harvesting, and sewage treatment are getting preference from both buyers and tenants. Lower maintenance bills and healthier living make these features more than just a marketing line.\n\nIntegrated townships that combine homes, offices, retail, schools, and healthcare inside one campus are gaining traction on the outskirts. They reduce commute stress and create a self-contained lifestyle for young families and elderly parents. Co-living and managed rental communities near IT and college hubs also remain relevant for investors who want ready rental demand without managing day-to-day tenants themselves.\n\n## Tips to Buy Property in Bangalore Safely [...] ₹50 Lakhs – ₹1 Crore\n\nIn Bangalore, this band is the most popular among end users. In this slab, a lot of working couples, IT workers, and small business owners search for 2 or tiny 3 BHK apartments. Options include established communities in South and West Bangalore with somewhat lower unit sizes, as well as active and almost finished projects in East and North Bangalore. You can balance location, project quality, amenities, and loan eligibility in this range without going above your EMI. For serious property purchasers, the majority of well-known township projects, communal living alternatives, and metro-linked corridors begin to become accessible in this category.\n\nAbove ₹1 Crore","score":0.15676242,"raw_content":null,"id":"15206b-05"},{"url":"https://www.99acres.com/articles/homebuyers-guide-to-choose-right-amenities.html","title":"Tips to select right amenities for your property","content":"Swimming pool; Gym; Walking/Jogging track; Play area; Club house; Rooftop garden; Open deck; Sky lounge; Spa and salon; Concierge services; Restaurants; Party","score":0.1449098,"raw_content":null,"id":"83abd3-06"},{"url":"https://www.mahindralifespaces.com/blog/impact-location-and-amenities-on-property-value","title":"Location vs Amenities: What Impacts Property Value More?","content":"Every project begins with location intelligence. Be it walk-to-work residences near business parks or homes in emerging corridors with strong future connectivity, site selection is driven by long-term growth and livability. Mahindra World City in Chennai, exemplify this vision by placing homes, workplaces, schools, and leisure zones within a single ecosystem.\n\nOn the amenity side, we go beyond checklists. From green-certified buildings to wellness-focused layouts and EV-ready infrastructure, we at Mahindra Lifespaces ensure that every space enhances daily life while staying future-ready. Projects are designed to reduce environmental impact, enhance community living, and deliver better rental and resale potential over time. [...] Pro Tip: When evaluating a property, look for upcoming infrastructure projects like metro extensions or business parks. These developments can significantly boost future appreciation.\n\n## How Amenities Influence Homebuyer Decisions\n\nModern homebuyers look beyond square footage—they want a lifestyle that supports convenience, wellness, and a sense of community. In today’s market, amenities have become key value enhancers, playing a direct role in how people perceive a home’s worth. Here’s how amenities impact the property value and desirability:\n\n### 1. Amenities Create Lifestyle Appeal\n\n Features like clubhouses, swimming pools, gyms, and green spaces enhance daily living.\n Homebuyers, especially families, prefer projects offering all-in-one convenience.\n\n### 2. Perception Drives Value [...] Connectivity: Proximity to metro stations, schools, hospitals, and business hubs ensures daily convenience. For example, homes within 1 km of metro stations in cities like Bengaluru or Delhi appreciate faster over time.\n Livability: A livable location cuts commute times, allowing more time for family, work, and leisure.\n Long-Term Equity: Properties in well-connected areas hold their value better, even during market fluctuations.\n\nIn terms of real estate valuation in India, the correct location often builds long-term equity. Amenities might grab your attention, but it’s the living environment that keeps a property's value steady over time.","score":0.13259341,"raw_content":null,"id":"dfb829-07"}],"response_time":3.19,"request_id":"20f8bb54-79ce-4e13-adc1-617a26e798fc"}